{"In getGroupIdsWithViewPermission(), groupResource.getId() is passed to hasPermission which expects a resource name (uses resourceStore.findByName), not an ID, so the permission check will often fail to resolve the resource": 0.9434221386909485, "getGroupIdsWithViewPermission() returns authorization resource IDs instead of group IDs (GroupModel IDs) that callers expect for user queries": 0.9589871764183044, "testManageGroupMembership only tests user-level MANAGE_GROUP_MEMBERSHIP permission but doesn't verify the new group-level MANAGE_MEMBERSHIP and MANAGE_MEMBERS scopes are actually wired into membership management": 0.47555989027023315, "Test is missing a case where user lacks user-level MANAGE_GROUP_MEMBERSHIP but has group-level MANAGE_MEMBERS/MANAGE_MEMBERSHIP, verifying joinGroup/leaveGroup succeed based solely on group permissions": 0.21947845816612244, "Test is missing a negative case where only MANAGE_MEMBERSHIP (no MANAGE_MEMBERS) is granted on the group to assert the intended difference between these two scopes": 0.7291091680526733}